# FastAPI Endpoint Patterns

## `def` vs `async def`

- Use plain `def` when the endpoint calls synchronous/blocking code (file reads, DB operations via SQLModel, no `await`)
- FastAPI automatically runs `def` endpoints in a threadpool — this is the correct approach for blocking I/O
- `async def` with blocking code **blocks the event loop** and freezes all concurrent requests
- Only use `async def` when all I/O inside uses `await` (e.g., `httpx.AsyncClient`, async DB drivers)
- Reference: [FastAPI async docs](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/async/#path-operation-functions)
